Well, I finally did a wizard, after at least 50 or so incarnations.  The big
turning points were a lot of early luck, namely a magic lamp, bag of
holding, and luckstone, all before minetown.   Got SDSM, and teleportis (had
a = of teleport control).  Anyway, not a whole lot to talk about, this game
took quite a while mostly because I found an altar on the level above the
castle.  After a little sac fest, using up my scrolls, wands, bags of
tricks, etc., I got the spellbook of create monster, and with the eye and
Int of 25, I was creating a ton of monsters.  Eventually got nearly every
spell from sacrificing or polypiling.  As far as conducts, I tried to go
lighter on the genocide (I usually genocide h, L, disenchanters, and ;, this
time I only genocided L, and only because last time I lost my wizard on
astral because of an arch-lich blocking my way).  I *almost* got away
without polyselfing, but I had no means of levitation, so I put on my rings
of polymorph and control to enter the castle.  I suppose I could have gone
in the front, or perhaps have waited till I had acquired the spell of
levitation, but oh well, I polyselfed into a vamp lord.  BTW, how do you
open the drawbridge?  I was divinely given the tune, so I walked up near the
bridge, pulled out a harp (or maybe horn) and said to play the passtune,
which did nothing.... odd....


